1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:00,638
What is life,

2
00:00:00,662 --> 00:00:00,962
really?

3
00:00:01,388 --> 00:00:02,400
Bach starts with the cell.

4
00:00:02,812 --> 00:00:05,325
A cell is an extraordinary molecular machine.

5
00:00:05,738 --> 00:00:08,625
It harvests energy from its environment and uses

6
00:00:08,638 --> 00:00:10,550
it to keep its own structure in order,

7
00:00:10,925 --> 00:00:12,475
pushing back against entropy.

8
00:00:12,888 --> 00:00:13,575
In a sense,

9
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,712
a cell is a biological computer,

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,862
running a program that keeps it alive.

11
00:00:18,288 --> 00:00:20,488
When billions of cells come together to form

12
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,050
a plant,

13
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:22,788
an animal or a human,

14
00:00:23,175 --> 00:00:24,788
they need rules to cooperate.

15
00:00:25,212 --> 00:00:26,588
Something has to coordinate them,

16
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:29,000
so that they act as one organism and

17
00:00:29,012 --> 00:00:29,850
not as a crowd.

18
00:00:30,262 --> 00:00:32,025
And here Bach makes one of his most

19
00:00:32,038 --> 00:00:33,100
surprising claims.

20
00:00:33,525 --> 00:00:35,662
He says that when ancient cultures talked about

21
00:00:35,675 --> 00:00:38,062
spirit, they were pointing at something real.

22
00:00:38,488 --> 00:00:40,225
Spirit is an old word for what we

23
00:00:40,238 --> 00:00:41,875
would now call an operating system.

24
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,350
It is the software that runs an autonomous

25
00:00:44,362 --> 00:00:47,300
robot, the organizing pattern that makes a body

26
00:00:47,312 --> 00:00:48,088
act as one.

27
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,450
A plant has something like a spirit that

28
00:00:50,462 --> 00:00:51,362
links its cells.

29
00:00:51,775 --> 00:00:52,962
An ecosystem has one.

30
00:00:53,375 --> 00:00:53,900
You have one.

31
00:00:54,312 --> 00:00:56,025
And it does not stop at the individual.

32
00:00:56,512 --> 00:01:00,038
Families, companies, religions and nations are higher level

33
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:01,088
operating systems.

34
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,275
They coordinate millions of people,

35
00:01:03,638 --> 00:01:06,100
the way your mind coordinates billions of cells.

36
00:01:06,512 --> 00:01:07,812
A beehive works like this.

37
00:01:08,225 --> 00:01:09,300
So does a civilization.

38
00:01:09,725 --> 00:01:11,838
We like to think of ourselves as independent

39
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:14,175
heroes, but in many ways we are cells

40
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:15,850
inside a superorganism.

41
00:01:16,262 --> 00:01:18,725
And a superorganism does not care about any

42
00:01:18,738 --> 00:01:19,438
single cell.

43
00:01:19,862 --> 00:01:21,688
It cares about what keeps the whole system

44
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:21,975
running.

45
00:01:22,412 --> 00:01:23,825
Think about how strange that is.

46
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,375
The beliefs you defend,

47
00:01:25,738 --> 00:01:27,637
the rules you follow without thinking,

48
00:01:28,075 --> 00:01:29,788
even the things you find beautiful.

49
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,100
Many of them were installed by the larger

50
00:01:32,112 --> 00:01:33,525
system you were born into.

51
00:01:33,938 --> 00:01:36,137
That raises the most personal question of all.

52
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:38,450
If you are software running on a primate

53
00:01:38,462 --> 00:01:38,812
body,

54
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,075
what happens to you when the body stops?
